            <ArticleTitle>Trigeminal neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>198-203</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe trigeminal neuralgia (TN) is probably the most excruciating pain experienced in the orofacial region. Apart from the primary idiopathic form (ITN), this lancinating pain may be secondary to a range of underlying organic diseases (STN). Diagnosis requires differentiation of these and elimination of other causes of orofacial pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
